.\" unlink.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX unlink(1) utility, which
.\" this tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/UNLINK.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/UNLINK.
.TH UNLINK 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
unlink \- call the unlink function
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Unlink
is not provided on maux.
rm(1) already removes a directory entry the same way, so a
separate unlink utility is not shipped.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
rm(1)
